A||||5||286SE'S||Registration Fees 2M4 vs 2M6||||5||
Z||000000||286SE'S||09-11-2000||04:33 PM||||As you may have guessed by my username I have 2 1986 SE's. The cars are twins except for the engines, one is a 4, other is a 6.<BR>I just got the registration renewals this past week and the 2M4 is $52 and the 2M6 is<BR>$70. Does anybody know why the 6 cylinder car would cost more? I know this is the crazy California DMV but do other multiple Fiero families in any state notice a difference in their fees? I do not have personalized plates. Thanks.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||09-11-2000||04:41 PM||||Each state has their own rules on how to tax the car owner for registration fee.  In NY it was based on the weight of the car.<P>When I lived in California (many years ago) it was based on the value of the car.<P>One guy had a 56 Buick and plates cost $17/year and a (71 new at the time)240Z and the plates were $280/year.<P>The V6 is worth more than the 4.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gold-86SE||09-11-2000||04:53 PM||||<BR>Since Cally is big on "environmental emissions" the wonderful government may be making the assumption that a six cylinder puts out more emissions that the four cylinder, regardless of age or maintenance.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Gold-86SE (Fiero Collector)||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-11-2000||05:19 PM||||Mine all cost the same to register here in PA, but the insurance company gets me for a high power to weight ratio on my V6's.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||09-11-2000||05:53 PM||||I live in GA. <BR>My 88 coupe and my Formula are close enough that they could be called the same. Same with insurance. They DO make a distinction for a GT, though. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||09-11-2000||07:43 PM||||Nothing personal, but you guys live in crappy states. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Here in Indiana, they go by age and value (NADA, I assume).  Anything over 10 years old is the same.  My insurance company (Progressive) <B>did</B> charge me for for my GT.  12 bucks a year more, to be exact.  Couldn't really complain.||||reg||1
